Package: gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
Architecture: any
Section: plugins
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: GStreamer plugins from the "good" set
 GStreamer is a streaming media framework, based on graphs of filters
 which operate on media data.  Its plugin-based architecture means that
 new data types or processing capabilities can be added simply by
 installing new plug-ins.
 .
 This package contains the elements of the "good" set: the Matroska,
 FLV and RTP demuxers, the VP8 and VP9 codecs, the FLAC, Speex, WavPack,
 AMR, MP3, AAC and Shout elements.
 .
 This build has no Qt and no GTK video sinks: video is played by mpv
 and by labwc. It also has no PulseAudio, V4L2 and OSSv4 elements.
 .
 Upstream 1.28.7 builds no shared libraries in this plugin set (its
 gst-libs/gst directory contains only a header), so there is nothing
 for libgstreamer-plugins-good1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-good1.0-dev
 or gir1.2-gst-plugins-good-1.0 to carry: those binary packages are not
 published. The Matroska, RTP, RTSP and tag helper libraries this set
 uses come from gstreamer1.0-plugins-base.
